---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import MoreTools from '../components/MoreTools.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { LIMITS } from '../lib/invoice';
const title = `About ${site.name}`;
const description = `How ${site.name} calculates totals and rounding, which tax modes it supports, and exactly what is stored and where.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="container container--narrow section prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'About', url: '/about/' }]} />
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated: {site.updated}</p>
    <p>{site.description}</p>

    <h2>Methodology: rounding</h2>
    <p>
      Every money amount is rounded to the invoicing currency's minor unit — 2 decimal places for most currencies, 0 for
      currencies like JPY or KRW, 3 for currencies like KWD or BHD, per ISO 4217 — the moment it is produced: per line,
      per discount share, per tax line. Rounding uses round-half-away-from-zero on a float-noise-corrected value (so
      0.1 + 0.2 never shows as 0.30000000000000004). Totals are sums of already-rounded parts, so every printed line adds
      up exactly to the printed total — there is no separate "rounding adjustment" line to reconcile.
    </p>

    <h2>Methodology: tax modes</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Exclusive tax</strong> (the default) adds tax on top of the line amount: <code>tax = amount × rate</code>.{' '}
      <strong>Inclusive tax</strong> treats the line amount as already containing tax and backs it out:{' '}
      <code>taxable = amount ÷ (1 + rate)</code>, <code>tax = amount − taxable</code>. Each line item can carry its own tax
      rate; the document groups and subtotals tax by rate. A global discount (percentage or fixed amount, capped at the
      subtotal) is allocated across lines in proportion to each line's net amount before tax is calculated on the
      discounted amount, so tax is never charged on a discount that was not actually applied.
    </p>

    <h2>Methodology: due dates &amp; numbering</h2>
    <p>
      "Net N" terms add N calendar days to the issue date (see the <a href={withBase('/guide/net-30-payment-terms/')}>Net 30 guide</a>{' '}
      for a worked table); "Custom" keeps whatever date you set. Document numbers auto-increment per document type
      (invoice / quote / receipt / credit note) using a counter kept in your browser, incrementing the trailing digit run
      of the last number used and preserving zero-padding (see the <a href={withBase('/guide/invoice-numbering/')}>numbering guide</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your current draft, saved documents, saved clients and the per-type numbering counters are written only to this
        browser's <code>localStorage</code> — never to a server. Clearing your browser's site data removes them.</li>
      <li>A logo you upload is kept as a data URL in local storage; it is included in a share link only if it is smaller
        than {Math.round(LIMITS.logoShareBytes / 1024)} KB, to keep links a reasonable length.</li>
      <li>The <strong>share link</strong> ("Share this document") encodes the entire document — client, items, totals,
        template — compressed into the URL fragment after <code>#</code> using the open-source <code>lz-string</code>{' '}
        library. Text after <code>#</code> is never sent to any server by the browser, but anyone who has the link can
        open and read the document, so only share it with people who should see it. There is no database and no account
        behind this feature.</li>
      <li>Nothing is sent to us. If analytics are enabled, they are aggregate and cookieless — see the{' '}
        <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> for exactly what that means.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>This is not tax, legal or accounting advice. The invoice template pages summarise commonly cited requirements
        (e.g. UK VAT invoice content, EU reverse-charge wording, India GST fields) with links to official sources — always
        confirm current rates and thresholds there before relying on a document for filing.</li>
      <li>"Download as image (PNG)" is not implemented yet; use "Download PDF" (print to PDF), which is fully supported.</li>
      <li>There is no cloud backup — use "Export JSON backup" in the editor's Saved panel periodically if you rely on the
        saved-documents list, especially before clearing browser data or switching devices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Licensing &amp; attribution</h2>
    <p>
      Built with open-source libraries used under their own licences: Astro, Preact (MIT), <code>lz-string</code> (MIT,
      URL-safe document compression) and <code>qrcode</code> (MIT, pay-link QR codes). No third-party invoice templates,
      images or fonts requiring paid licensing are used; UI text is original.
    </p>

    <h2>Who maintains it</h2>
    <p>
      Built and maintained by <a href={site.author.url} rel="noopener">{site.author.name}</a>. Launched {site.launched}.
      Found a bug, an incorrect figure, or a stale source link? <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Get in touch</a> — data
      corrections are the fastest fixes we make.
    </p>
  </article>

  <section class="container">
    <MoreTools />
  </section>
</Base>
